In situation I, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =100, \\\\ 5%\\cdot N & =0.05\\cdot 500 \\\\  & =25 \\\\  & <100.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  the sample size is more than $5%$ of the population size, we *cannot* approximate the distribution of $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\n- In situation II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =60 \\\\  & \\le 5%\\cdot N \\\\  & =0.05\\cdot 1\\,500 \\\\  & =75\\,✓ \\\\ np & =60(0.90) \\\\  & =54 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =60(1-0.90) \\\\  & =6 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can approximate the distribution of $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\n- In situation III, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =40 \\\\  & \\le 5%\\cdot N \\\\  & =0.05\\cdot 1\\,500 \\\\  & =75\\,✓ \\\\ np & =40(0.9) \\\\  & =36 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =40(1-0.9) \\\\  & =4 \\\\  & ≯5.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $n(1-p)≯5,$ we *cannot* approximate the distribution of $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41537c58-9c96-5e6c-b0e6-778ebecb212c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Situations When the CLT for Proportions is Appropriate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd46750-aab1-5ab4-8f35-4bb7abe41d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501490} {:answer/id #uuid "508c1697-4000-5926-99b2-497ea4d6c810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501612} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad952b8-2ed2-584a-967d-7f752886a23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501664} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c31986-9c09-50b3-be41-6a9593a36e04" :answer